---
.title = "Build with ZML",
.description = "The framework path: from a runnable example to your own model.",
.date = .date("2026-11-06T00:00:00"),
.layout = "content.shtml",
---
ZML provides the inference framework and compilation machinery for model
applications. Its public project uses Zig, MLIR, and Bazel.

Follow the [ZML quickstart]($link.page('zml/quickstart')) to build and run MNIST
on CPU. Continue to [Build and run with Bazel]($link.page('zml/build-and-run'))
for accelerator flags, LLM examples, and packaging.

# [Follow the model lifecycle]($heading.id('follow-the-model-lifecycle'))

Read [ZML concepts]($link.page('zml/concepts')) for tensors, shapes, and dimension tags.
Use the [Tensor reference]($link.page('zml/api/tensor')) to look up model operations
and the [Exe reference]($link.page('zml/api/exe')) for calls that run a compiled model.
Use the [first model guide]($link.page('zml/first-model')) to build a tagged
linear layer. Then [load and inspect checkpoints]($link.page('zml/checkpoints'))
for pretrained weights and [run ZML across devices]($link.page('zml/sharding'))
to partition work across a device mesh.

```=html
<figure class="execution-diagram" aria-label="ZML model execution">
  <div class="execution-paths">
    <ol class="execution-path" role="list" aria-label="Compile the model">
      <li class="execution-node">
        <strong>Zig model code</strong>
        <span><code>forward</code> and symbolic tensor shapes and types</span>
      </li>
      <li class="execution-node">
        <strong>Compile for the selected backend</strong>
        <span>Trace to StableHLO and compile through PJRT</span>
      </li>
      <li class="execution-artifact">Executable</li>
    </ol>
    <ol class="execution-path" role="list" aria-label="Prepare runtime data">
      <li class="execution-node">
        <strong>Checkpoint weights and inputs</strong>
        <span>Weight values from Safetensors and input data</span>
      </li>
      <li class="execution-node">
        <strong>Fill backend buffers</strong>
        <span>Load weight values and transfer inputs to the selected backend</span>
      </li>
      <li class="execution-artifact">Buffers</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="execution-run">
    <strong>Run on the selected backend</strong>
    <span>Call the executable with the weight and input buffers to produce output tensors.</span>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Checkpoint metadata can supply weight shapes and data types for the symbolic tensors used during compilation.</figcaption>
</figure>
```

The [upstream ZML repository](https://github.com/zml/zml) contains examples and
framework documentation. A reproducible procedure needs a selected source
revision and a recorded environment.

# [Choose the server path when appropriate]($heading.id('choose-the-server-path-when-appropriate'))

For an application that calls a model over HTTP, continue to
[LLMD]($link.page('llmd')). For service management, continue to
[Operations]($link.page('operations')).
